185	GRAPHITI_MCP_INSTRUCTIONS = """
186	Welcome to Graphiti MCP - a memory service for AI agents built on a knowledge graph. Graphiti performs well
187	with dynamic data such as user interactions, changing enterprise data, and external information.
188	
189	Graphiti transforms information into a richly connected knowledge network, allowing you to 
190	capture relationships between concepts, entities, and information. The system organizes data as episodes 
191	(content snippets), nodes (entities), and facts (relationships between entities), creating a dynamic, 
192	queryable memory store that evolves with new information. Graphiti supports multiple data formats, including 
193	structured JSON data, enabling seamless integration with existing data pipelines and systems.
194	
195	Facts contain temporal metadata, allowing you to track the time of creation and whether a fact is invalid 
196	(superseded by new information).
197	
198	Key capabilities:
199	1. Add episodes (text, messages, or JSON) to the knowledge graph with the add_episode tool
200	2. Search for nodes (entities) in the graph using natural language queries with search_nodes
201	3. Find relevant facts (relationships between entities) with search_facts
202	4. Retrieve specific entity edges or episodes by UUID
203	5. Manage the knowledge graph with tools like delete_episode, delete_entity_edge, and clear_graph
204	
205	The server connects to a database for persistent storage and uses language models for certain operations. 
206	Each piece of information is organized by group_id, allowing you to maintain separate knowledge domains.
207	
208	When adding information, provide descriptive names and detailed content to improve search quality. 
209	When searching, use specific queries and consider filtering by group_id for more relevant results.
210	
211	For optimal performance, ensure the database is properly configured and accessible, and valid 
212	API keys are provided for any language model operations.
213	"""
214	
